     Nah, I looked through the source on this and found 
that your luck increases by two and your alignment by 
five.  On the other hand, if you're *not* chaotic, and you 
don't get killed by the demon lord, you lose five luck 
points, your u.ugangr is increased by THREE (meaning you 
have to find three largish corpses to appease your God, 
instead of the usual just one.  On the other hand, being 
!chaotic, your corpses don't have to be all that big), and 
your god does something nasty to you as well.  Not a 
particularly nice situation to be in. 
     Apart from the annoying friendly monster, it's 
actually a *good* thing for a chaotic player to do, 
especially if he/she has a luckstone.  Five human 
sacrifices and you've got maximum luck, and that makes 
prayers very helpful.
 
